  "title": "Calotype photography in Britain and France",
  "html": "<div class=\"task note-list\"><h3>Questions 31–40</h3><p class=\"instructions\">Complete the notes. Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</p><h4 class=\"task-title\">Calotype photography in Britain and France</h4><div class=\"form-row section-heading\">From Daguerreotype to Calotype</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>Daguerreotype was the first commercial photographic process.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>Daguerreotype had a problem: the use of copper made it <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"31\" id=\"q31\" name=\"q31\" placeholder=\"31\" aria-label=\"Question 31\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>William Talbot began looking for an alternative approach in the 1840s.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>Talbot was not originally a photographer but an artist who specialised in <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"32\" id=\"q32\" name=\"q32\" placeholder=\"32\" aria-label=\"Question 32\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>Talbot used paper instead of copper.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>These calotype photographs were more <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"33\" id=\"q33\" name=\"q33\" placeholder=\"33\" aria-label=\"Question 33\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"> because they weren’t so sharp.</div><div class=\"form-row section-heading\">French Calotype</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>In 1851, the first society for photographers was created.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>Gustave Le Gray became fascinated by calotype photography.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>He carried out experiments and produced the first <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"34\" id=\"q34\" name=\"q34\" placeholder=\"34\" aria-label=\"Question 34\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"> using a camera.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>He developed equipment that was easier to use outside the <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"35\" id=\"q35\" name=\"q35\" placeholder=\"35\" aria-label=\"Question 35\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>Calotype became famous because Le Gray produced <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"36\" id=\"q36\" name=\"q36\" placeholder=\"36\" aria-label=\"Question 36\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"> about it.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>People thought photography was more reliable than drawing.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>It was used to record the work done on old <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"37\" id=\"q37\" name=\"q37\" placeholder=\"37\" aria-label=\"Question 37\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>Photography was not ‘art’, according to <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"38\" id=\"q38\" name=\"q38\" placeholder=\"38\" aria-label=\"Question 38\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">.</div><div class=\"form-row section-heading\">Summary</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>Photography was thought of as a <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"39\" id=\"q39\" name=\"q39\" placeholder=\"39\" aria-label=\"Question 39\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">, so reflected the culture of the 1850s.</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>The use of new materials, particularly <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"40\" id=\"q40\" name=\"q40\" placeholder=\"40\" aria-label=\"Question 40\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">, led to new techniques.</div></div>",
